**Version**: 0.3
**Created**: 2026-07-07
**Status**: Draft — ComposeBus pattern-subscription primitive + transport filtering (in-process + MQTT operational; CAN binding designed). **§5 added 2026-07-28 (design convention — David's rulings):** the PUBLISHER-side reciprocal of the subscriber filter — a namespace is a CAN frame ID, so publish granular semantic events one-per-meaning ([CXC-PS-GRANULARITY]); publish meaning you OWN, never consumer commands ([CXC-PS-SEMANTIC-OWNERSHIP], exemplar: DRADIS `contact_identified` → DY-SV5F soundboard reactor, never `audio/cue`); default external emit ≤ 1 Hz decoupled from internal tick ([CXC-PS-RATE]). Named anti-patterns: fat-periodic-broadcast + consumer-coupled-command + emit-coupled-to-internal-tick. Compliance C9–C13 added. **§5a added 2026-08-11 (defect-driven — David's console message reached the Intelligence twice with a PROVEN-SINGLE relay):** the contract said only WHICH namespaces arrive, never HOW MANY TIMES, so nothing forbade double delivery — [CXC-PS-EXACTLY-ONCE] (one publish = exactly one invocation per registration, transport-topology-independent) and [CXC-PS-NO-SELF-ECHO] (a bus must not re-dispatch its own emission returning over a broadcast transport; MQTT 3.1.1 has no `noLocal`). Both mechanisms measured on the live broker. Compliance C14–C15 added; [CXC-IC-CHANNEL]'s IC-C15 amended, its singleton being necessary-but-not-sufficient.
